BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//hello world//almanac//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
METHOD:PUBLISH
X-WR-CALNAME:hello world
X-WR-CALDESC:The observances of a small world made of punctuation\, slowed 
 down to fit a diary. A day there takes about as long as reading a sentence
 \; these have been kept at your pace instead\, as a courtesy\, and repeat 
 for as long as you let them.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:starday@helloworldandthen.com
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19700104
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19700105
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=SU
SUMMARY:Starday
DESCRIPTION:The seventh day of the week and not a weekend\, the world havin
 g none. Observed by carrying on exactly as usual. If you were going to do 
 something today\, that is the observance.
LOCATION:The world. Not yours\; the small one.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:shade@helloworldandthen.com
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART:19700115T120000
DTEND:19700115T120400
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=15
SUMMARY:The Shade
DESCRIPTION:The At comes out in front and stands in the light\, and a small
  round night crosses the day from west to east. It lasts about four of you
 r minutes\, which is generous. Nobody underneath looks up. You may.
LOCATION:The world. Not yours\; the small one.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:back@helloworldandthen.com
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19700101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19700102
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=1
SUMMARY:The At goes round the back
DESCRIPTION:For reasons of its own. It will come back looking exactly as it
  did. No action is required\, and none is possible.
LOCATION:The world. Not yours\; the small one.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:land@helloworldandthen.com
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART:19700113T030000
DTEND:19700113T030100
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYDAY=2TU
SUMMARY:The Caret sights land
DESCRIPTION:And turns away. The crew regard this as a route. Entered here a
 t three in the morning so as not to disturb anyone\, including the land.
LOCATION:The world. Not yours\; the small one.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:flags@helloworldandthen.com
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19700309
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19700310
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:Flag Day!
DESCRIPTION:For the Exclamations. The world holds nine. Plant a tenth today
  and the oldest quietly falls over\, as on any other day. The exclamation 
 mark in the title is not enthusiasm\; it is a flag.
LOCATION:The world. Not yours\; the small one.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:poles-n@helloworldandthen.com
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19700621
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19700622
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:Midwinter at the Asterisk Caps (south)
DESCRIPTION:The world has no tilt and so no seasons. Midwinter is kept anyw
 ay\, once for each pole\, to be fair. The ice is the same as yesterday. Ea
 ch flake remains a footnote.
LOCATION:The world. Not yours\; the small one.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:poles-s@helloworldandthen.com
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19701221
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19701222
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:Midwinter at the Asterisk Caps (north)
DESCRIPTION:See the other one. On the dark side the asterisks dim to plus s
 igns\; this is the only arithmetic the planet does\, and it is not doing i
 t for the occasion.
LOCATION:The world. Not yours\; the small one.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dittos@helloworldandthen.com
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19701001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19701002
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:Cloud expected
DESCRIPTION:The Dittos come over from the west in rows. This is true of eve
 ry day\, but it seemed wrong for a calendar to have no weather in it at al
 l. Same as above. Same as above.
LOCATION:The world. Not yours\; the small one.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stop@helloworldandthen.com
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19701231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19710101
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:Full Stop
DESCRIPTION:Sentences end here. Expect a long pause\, then land\, or mornin
 g\, whichever comes first.
LOCATION:The world. Not yours\; the small one.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:began@helloworldandthen.com
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19700101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19700102
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SUMMARY:The beginning of time (observed)
DESCRIPTION:Time on the world began when you arrived\, which is a different
  day for everyone and no good to a calendar. This date is a compromise\, b
 orrowed from the machines\, who all believe it.
LOCATION:The world. Not yours\; the small one.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:year@helloworldandthen.com
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:19720229
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:19720301
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=2;BYMONTHDAY=29
SUMMARY:A year\, if there were years
DESCRIPTION:There are none\, the world having nothing to go around. This is
  the day on which your calendar comes nearest to admitting the same diffic
 ulty.
LOCATION:The world. Not yours\; the small one.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
